{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Behold the hand of YHWH is upon your livestock that is in the field</b> — He warned them about what is present, for most of the livestock is in the field, but the pestilence was also upon the livestock that is in the house, as it says (Exodus 9:6), \"And all the livestock of Egypt died.\" And it is possible that because every shepherd of sheep was an abomination to Egypt (Genesis 46:34), they would keep them separated from the cities, except when they used the horses for riding and the donkeys for carrying loads. And so the livestock was far from Egypt, in the field of the border of Goshen, and the livestock of Egypt and the livestock of Israel would intermingle in the grazing place, and therefore it was necessary to say, <b>And YHWH will make a distinction between the livestock of Egypt and the livestock of Israel</b>. Or, because the pestilence, resulting from a change in the air, would naturally spread throughout the entire province, but HaShem performed a wonder with them to distinguish."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {0 "The lemma head translates only the phrase from Exodus 9:3a, but Ramban's Hebrew here also incorporates text from Exodus 9:4 as a second bolded lemma within the same comment; both are preserved."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:16:29.290523656Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}